{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"APPROVED RP-04 decision: static-secret rotation for long-running processes is restart/redeploy based. Short-lived CLI processes receive current startup environment; long-running MCP/server processes must restart after a static secret changes; container workloads must restart/redeploy so the platform reinjects the current value, including ECS new-task/forced-deployment behavior. Rebar will not poll environment, retrieve/refresh SSM, watch secret files, or maintain a hot-reload secret cache. If the old credential is revoked before restart, operations fail as authentication failures without fallback to another ambient or anonymous identity. Native temporary/workload credentials remain SDK-owned and may refresh in process. Added implementation verification obligations for new process, long-running process, post-restart, revoked old credential, and native refresh cases. Gitleaks found no leaks."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786937159552458001,"uuid":"2240891a-029d-4bc4-86fb-081626426913"}